\f0\fs24 \cf0 -The PCB schematic and layout were designed in Kicad.\
-Once manufactured I hand soldered the SMD components to the board and tested.\
-The PCB was measured in Onshape so I could design a base\
-The acrylic base was first drawn out in Onshape, printed on paper to ensure the parts would fit, and then it was sent to the CO2 laser cutter for manufacturing.\
-Once the base was made, the PCB, batteries, motors, encoder, and wheels were attached to the base.\
-The STM32 program provided by our professor, I used STM32CubeIDE and STM32CubeProgrammer to build, and flash the PCB. \
-Once the program was on the board I tested it by connecting my phone to the ESP8266, and go to the ip address in a browser.\
-Upon testing the robot works as intended. One issue I noticed was the ESP8266 app would sometimes disconnect, but would reconnect a few moments later. \
